# Competency question: "Which properties frame a p-value — what makes P(T >= t | H0)
# unambiguous?" Exercises the p-value framing object properties: a math:PValue carries its
# magnitude (math:pValue), the null it is computed under (math:nullHypothesis), the
# distribution of the statistic under that null (math:nullDistribution), the statistic driving
# it (math:testStatistic), the tail it is measured over (math:tailDefinition), its enumerated
# sidedness (math:alternativeSidedness), and — for multiplicity — the adjustment applied
# (math:pValueAdjustment) over a comparison family (math:multipleComparisonFamily). The query
# projects each PREDICATE on the p-value, scoped to the math: namespace. Over the fixture the
# answer is exactly the eight p-value-framing property edges.
PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX ex:   <http://example.org/math/>

SELECT ?prop ?object WHERE {
    ex:pval ?prop ?object .
    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?prop), "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/"))
}
ORDER BY ?prop ?object
